class Solution:
    def maxDepth(self, root: Optional[TreeNode]) -> int:
    if root is None:
         return 0
    m = self.maxDepth(root.left)
    n = self.maxDepth(root.right)

    return max(m,n) + 1

algorithm:
in this problem we were given to find out the maximum depth of the given binary tree 
so we have to caluculate the subtree to the node 
for that we use recursive function which calls out the no. of nodes present in the each subtree
maxDepth is used to bring out the maximum length of the subtree and out of both left and right subtree we want the maximum value 
and finally + 1 is added to the max value returned such that current node is included
